      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Hosmer House, a 1760 saltbox on the National Register, now serves as a restored museum of early Acton life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.actonhistoricalsociety.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "East Acton grew around its 19th‑century train station, becoming a commercial hub before cars shifted development to Route 2A.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acton%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Acton Historical Society, a volunteer 501(c)(3), preserves town history through its Jenks Library, which houses maps, photos, and drawings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
